+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>Evidence & open questions · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/atlas-hierarchy-v0.2.css"><script src="/assets/atlas-hierarchy-v0.2.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="editorial"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/"><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/"><span>02</span>Foundations</a><a href="/research/"><span>03</span>Research programmes</a><a href="/evidence/" aria-current="page"><span>04</span>Evidence & open questions</a><a href="/papers/"><span>05</span>Papers & reading</a><a href="/archive/"><span>06</span>Research archive</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><div class="atlas-utilities"><a href="/updates/">Updates</a><a href="/sources/">Search sources</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribute</a></div><span class="status-dot"></span>Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>AI-assisted research<br>Review remains scope-specific</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">20 October 2026 UTC · CPC v0.1</div><h1>The clock must fit the physical plant.</h1><p class="lede">A component audit exposes a compatibility gate: slower filtered acquisition can require a substantially slower canonical LC plant.</p></div>
+<aside class="callout"><strong>Derived conditional · Hardware HOLD · Physical promotion 0</strong><p>Two elementary theorems establish clock–plant compatibility and filtered-history error. Ten exact controls and alternative SAC/FCAL budget replays pass. Supplier specifications are not measurements of an assembled apparatus; independent review remains pending.</p></aside>
+<div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/clock-plant-v0.1/UD_CLOCK_PLANT_COMPATIBILITY_v0.1.pdf">Read four-page theorem and audit PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/clock-plant-v0.1/UD_CLOCK_PLANT_COMPATIBILITY_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Download source package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/clock-plant-v0.1/IDENTIFICATION_PLAN_v0.1.json">Open identification plan</a></div>
+<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Slowing the clock is not a free adjustment.</h2><p>For each physical canonical pair, normalized plant coefficients satisfy αβ=t₀²/(LC). Their smallest possible common maximum is t₀/√(LC), achieved by balanced flux–charge scales. The inherited λ≤1 requirement therefore needs t₀≤min √(LC).</p><p>The timing allocation gives the other side: t₀ must be at least 400000 times the largest of output period, filter-history moment plus electronics latency, and actuator time constant. Both sides must hold on calibrated intervals.</p><p>The audited averaging-mode spacing yields a lower clock of 2048/5 seconds under this allocation. Every pair would then require LC≥4194304/25 seconds squared. A declared LC≤1 second squared envelope has no overlap. This is a restriction on the stated contract, not a universal impossibility result.</p></div></section>
+<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>A filtered sample contains history.</h2><p>The readout theorem bounds error by state speed times the absolute first age moment of the filter, plus bounded raw error times the absolute coefficient sum. Signed filter weights can have zero signed group delay and still carry nonzero history error.</p><p>Filter mode, coefficients, aperture times, startup tails, channel skew and output availability must be recorded. Typical RMS noise and an advertised bit count do not establish the required simultaneous reconstruction bound.</p></div></section>
+<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>A revised accuracy allocation passes mathematically.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Alternative supplied quantity</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td>Input reconstruction bound ν</td><td>1/100000</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Complete command error q</td><td>1/25000</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Tracking bound</td><td>29383/16000000</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Total continuous residual</td><td>149383/16000000 = 0.0093364375</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Slack below 1/100</td><td>10617/16000000</td></tr>
+</tbody></table><p>The alternative preserves the earlier conditional Gauss fault gaps and preload tolerance. It extends the valid earlier allocation; it does not replace its historical record. Actual noise, affine errors, drift, reference and driver errors must fit the remaining allowances.</p><p>The initial screen covers AD5791B, LTC2500-32 and an ADS127L21 alternative. All are candidates. Exact conditions and manufacturer links are in the audit; no part is admitted or selected for purchase.</p></div></section>
+<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>The required identification records are explicit.</h2><p>First return actual L, C, loading, canonical action and energy scales, and a nonempty clock interval. Next freeze the converter history and timing. Then provide traceable static calibration, simultaneous noise bounds, and independent actuator output and derivative records.</p><p>The actuator test must bound rₐ=(physical output derivative)/(physical pole)+output−held command on every relevant held segment, including one-sided transitions and glitches. Finite samples require a separate regularity and coverage certificate.</p><p>Release tracking, prehistory speed, range, slew and work remain required. Blinded nominal and fault runs follow only after the premises and attributable non-constructor review are recorded. No experiment has been performed.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/sampled-actuator/">Read the sampled-actuator theorem →</a></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public atlas</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
