-<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>Evidence & open questions · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/atlas-hierarchy-v0.2.css"><script src="/assets/atlas-hierarchy-v0.2.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="editorial"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/"><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/"><span>02</span>Foundations</a><a href="/research/"><span>03</span>Research programmes</a><a href="/evidence/" aria-current="page"><span>04</span>Evidence & open questions</a><a href="/papers/"><span>05</span>Papers & reading</a><a href="/archive/"><span>06</span>Research archive</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><div class="atlas-utilities"><a href="/updates/">Updates</a><a href="/sources/">Search sources</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribute</a></div><span class="status-dot"></span>Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>AI-assisted research<br>Review remains scope-specific</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="atlas-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Overview</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Evidence & open questions</span></div><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Evidence & open questions</div><h1>What is established?<br>What still needs a test?</h1><p class="lede">Finite mathematical checks, constructor executions and physical measurements answer different questions. The programme has no promoted physical identification.</p></div><div class="status-strip"><div>Physical promotion <b>0</b></div><div>Independent review <b>Scope-specific / pending or HOLD</b></div></div><article class="claim" id="canonical-map-v01"><div class="eyebrow">20 October 2026 UTC · Canonical map and component test 0.1</div><h2>The apparatus map now fixes action, energy and time</h2><p>The scaled canonical theorem gives ordinary flux–charge pairs the required opposite matter brackets and reciprocal gauge dynamics. Sixty-four exact checks pass. CD-1 specifies one instrumented four-link diamond, independent coupling witnesses, known-source injection and two analytically discriminating fault controls.</p><p>Engineering gates are proposed and require actual calibration and non-constructor review. Physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/canonical-map/">Read theorem and closed-diamond test →</a></article><article class="claim" id="finite-calibration-v01"><div class="eyebrow">20 October 2026 UTC · Finite calibration certificate 0.1</div><h2>CD-1 now has a conditional finite-calibration and fault budget</h2><p>Explicit physical port commands, a finite-cover theorem and an exact short-window uncertainty allocation separate the nominal law from two specified faults near model time 1/100. Controller input age has its own bound, separate from readout spacing.</p><p>Six-page theorem manuscript; exact constructor checks. Apparatus bounds OPEN, independent review pending, physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/finite-calibration/">Read the certificate and apparatus-return requirements →</a></article><article class="claim" id="sampled-actuator-v01"><div class="eyebrow">20 October 2026 UTC · Sampled actuator certificate 0.1</div><h2>A controller and finite-bandwidth actuator fit the CD-1 prefix budget conditionally</h2><p>The theorem budgets sample age, input and command error, actuator lag, preload and range. The illustrative total residual is exactly 145267/16000000, below 1/100, preserving the prior short-window fault gaps. Nine exact controls and an inherited-budget replay pass.</p><p>Actual components, identification and calibration remain OPEN; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/sampled-actuator/">Read the theorem and instrument requirements →</a></article><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Assess each result at its own level.</h2><div class="atlas-evidence-levels"><div><span>01 / Mathematics</span><h3>A declared finite object</h3><p>Exact algebra or a scoped proof on a specified carrier, metric and source convention.</p></div><div><span>02 / Computation</span><h3>A reproducible execution</h3><p>A frozen numerical or exact record with input hashes, tolerances and failure controls.</p></div><div><span>03 / Review</span><h3>An attributable challenge</h3><p>A non-constructor return bound to the exact claim or package, with its independence and scope.</p></div><div><span>04 / Correspondence</span><h3>An eligible physical test</h3><p>A calibrated map, units, uncertainty, baseline and a frozen independent acceptance rule.</p></div></div><p>The CRL-2 source proposal is preserved as a proposal. Publishing this hierarchy does not enact it or promote a scientific status.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=A21">Read the source proposal →</a><a class="text-link" href="/reconciliation/">Inspect source dispositions →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Current programme boundaries.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Programme</th><th>What the current record supports</th><th>What remains open</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Source, events and refinement</td><td>Conditional finite mechanisms, exact compatibility and nonselection results</td><td>Native source selection, preparation and a physical time/observable map</td></tr><tr id="observation-review-status"><td>Observation and estimation</td><td>Finite observability results and constructor certificates on declared records</td><td>Attributable external replay, uniform guarantees where claimed and physical metrology; review HOLD preserved</td></tr><tr><td>Action and stability</td><td>Declared action, scoped stability results and conditional preparation/error budgets</td><td>Realization and records meeting the complete experiment contract</td></tr><tr><td>Parity transport</td><td>Finite selected sector, typed transport identities and prospective numeric admission</td><td>Non-constructor review of the new contract, original attributable approval/raw output gaps and physical parity</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/research/">Read the programme map →</a><a class="text-link" href="/research-record/">Inspect the source-bound returns →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>A concrete bridge candidate, with a data boundary.</h2><div id="measurable-audit-v01"><p>A rank-one rotor–matter circuit emulator was selected for development. The published LC device is a partial benchmark: its oscillator links and chain do not implement the full UD Hamiltonian and required diamonds.</p><p>No audited dataset supplies every preparation, energy and source-work gate. The next proposed component experiment is a closed-diamond test with a calibrated measurement contract.</p><div class="atlas-grid"><a class="atlas-card" href="/evidence/measurable-audit/"><h3>Read the realization and dataset audit</h3><p>Selection, inspected records, mismatches and minimum experiment requirements.</p><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Read historical replication claims with their receipts.</h2><p>The historical parity record reports 12 in-scope passes and six failing controls from external-AI replication, with the permanent rider <em>transport consistency, not dynamical discovery</em>. Receipt linkage and the full ruling document are recovered; named or signed original approval and the raw-output commitment remain unresolved.</p><p>This is a source-recorded internal transport result. It is not independent-human review or a laboratory measurement, and the new prospective contract does not retroactively revise the old scores.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/research/parity/">Read the parity programme →</a><a class="text-link" href="/research-record/#custody">Inspect source and review custody →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">05</div><div><h2>What a physical return must contain.</h2><ol class="atlas-sequence"><li><strong>State the correspondence.</strong><span>Define the mathematical object, measured observable, units and calibration.</span></li><li><strong>Freeze the test.</strong><span>Specify baseline, exclusions, uncertainty budget, acceptance and failure rules before target exposure.</span></li><li><strong>Separate the evaluation.</strong><span>Record target custody, reviewer independence, negative results and the exact supported scope.</span></li></ol><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/contribution/">Choose a review or experiment gate →</a><a class="text-link" href="/archive/">Find the underlying evidence →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">06</div><div><h2>Applied programmes have separate evidence ledgers.</h2><div class="atlas-grid"><a class="atlas-card" href="https://mqm-research.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/"><h3>MQM</h3><p>Fault-aware quantum-code and controller research; hardware advantage needs its own evidence.</p><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="atlas-card" href="https://voxifold-systems.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/"><h3>Lattix Systems</h3><p>Spatial compute; equal-recall, equal-hardware benchmarks remain separate.</p><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section><span id="research-record-extension"></span></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public atlas</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
